{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/neidhardtiii"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"roleHeading":"Type Property","symbolKind":"property","extendedModule":"IvorTuning","title":"neidhardtIII","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE12neidhardtIIIAEvpZ","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(≈ 698.045 cents). Six fifths — A→E, B→F♯, F♯→C♯, C♯→A♭, E♭→B♭, B♭→F — are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma (≈ 700.000 cents). The remaining"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three fifths — E→B, A♭→E♭, F→C — are pure. The circle closes exactly:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"3×(1\/6) + 6×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Differs from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtII","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"only in the placement of the sixth-comma group on the flat side: E♭→B♭ is tempered"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"here where it is pure in Neidhardt II, and F→C is pure here where it is tempered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in Neidhardt II."}]}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724).","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtIII"},"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","title":"IvorTuning"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"TuningSystem","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem","abstract":[{"text":"A type that describes a musical tuning system.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem/neidhardtIII":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"neidhardtIII","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtIII","abstract":[{"text":"Neidhardt III (“Large City”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/neidhardtiii","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"abstract":[{"text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","title":"WellTemperament","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorTuning/docu